RF.put("questb:b26",{"8666":{"id":8666,"t":"Genesis Vest","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the the Husk of the Old God, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nHusk of the Old God C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Rebirth Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The unmentionable Old God slowly awakens from his slumber beneath Ahn'Qiraj. The terrible fate that awaits Azeroth could come in days or years; time has no meaning for beings of his power.\nWhen the stars are favorable, he will lash out against all living beings with terrible wrath. You must find him before then and find a way to bring his existence to an end.\nDo this and bring me a piece of his husk. I shall grant you armor no mortal has ever worn... armor fit for one who has slain a god!","rew":"You will receive:\nGenesis Vest\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"At his dwelling in Ahn'Qiraj, dread C'Thun awaits in slumber.","done":"I did not expect you to return from your attempt, ‹name›.\nYou've fulfilled a destiny greater than that of most immortal beings.\nBy slaying C'Thun you've not only saved all of Azeroth, you've also tipped the scales of cosmic events beyond your comprehension.\nAccept this breastplate as a symbol of the glory and burden that will come as a consequence of your actions.\nMay its power aid you in the challenges that await you, god-slayer!\nStart Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Druid Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8666\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Genesis Vest this quest\nBring the the Husk of the Old God, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nVethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8506":{"id":8506,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Purple Lotus!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 purple lotus to Master Nightsong at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Purple Lotus Elder Torntusk 40 % , Constrictor Vine 1.9 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 1.9 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 1.9 % and 4 more","desc":"Welcome back ‹class›. Our collection grows, but even now we have a need for additional purple lotus. If it is still within your power to gather more of the herb, I entreat you to do so and return them to me here.","rew":"You will receive:\n7 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.6,"y":32.5,"n":"Master Nightsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"6826":{"id":6826,"t":"Call of Air - Jeztor's Fleet","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stormpike Lieutenant's Flesh Winterax Mystic , Alliance Sentinel , Stormpike Mountaineer , Winterax Berserker and 4 more","back":"You've worked hard, ‹name›, but we have only just begun!\nMy War Riders must taste in the flesh of their targets. This will ensure a surgical strike against our enemies!\nMy fleet is the second most powerful in our air command. Thusly, they will strike at the more powerful of our adversaries. For this, then, they need the flesh of the Stormpike Lieutenants.\nMake haste, soldier!","done":"More! More! Bring more for they are soon to be ready!\nStart Wing Commander Jeztor Alterac Valley End Wing Commander Jeztor Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6826","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7386":{"id":7386,"t":"Crystal Cluster","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"null\n5 Storm Crystal Winterax Warrior 80 % , Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl 80 % , Alliance Sentinel 80 % , Stormpike Mountaineer 80 % and 4 more","desc":"There are times which you may be entrenched in battle for days or weeks on end. During those longer periods of activity you may end up collecting large clusters of the Frostwolf's storm crystals.\nThe Circle accepts such offerings, ‹name›.","back":"There are times which you may be entrenched in battle for days or weeks on end. During those longer periods of activity you may end up collecting large clusters of the Frostwolf's storm crystals.\nThe Circle accepts such offerings, ‹name›.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. I will use the power of these charms to augment the magic that has already been gathered. When enough power has been amassed, I shall focus the collected energies and call upon the Forest Lord to aid our cause.\nStart Arch Druid Renferal Alterac Valley End Arch Druid Renferal Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7386","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"666":{"id":666,"t":"Sunken Treasure","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Doctor Draxlegauge in Faldir's Cove wants you to collect 10 Elven Gems and return the Goggles of Gem Hunting once you are done.\n10 Elven Gem Calcified Elven Gem\nGoggles of Gem Hunting\nProvided: Goggles of Gem Hunting","desc":"The treasure has been on the sea floor so long that the gems have calcified into thick stone. But the power harnessed in these goggles will allow you to locate them easily.\nA little gnomish ingenuity goes a long way!\nSo borrow the Goggles of Gem Hunting, ‹name›, and see if you can collect some of the lost treasure for Captain O'Breen.\nI'd swim down there myself but...um...well, I have important scientific business to tend to up on the safe, dry land....er, yeah.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGnomish Zapper Servomechanic Sledgehammer\nExperience: 3,900\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"How did the goggles work? Did everything function properly? Adjustments can be made if necessary.\nOh, and I'll need those goggles back when you're done. I am sure Captain O'Breen will have many uses for them later on.","done":"Most superb, ‹name›! The Captain will be very pleased! And just wait until word gets back to Fleetmaster Seahorn!","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":33.9,"y":80.4,"n":"Doctor Draxlegauge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"7866":{"id":7866,"t":"Outrider Basic Care Package","lv":34,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nOutrider Basic Care Package\nExperience: 270\n+10 reputation with Warsong Outriders","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Warsong Gulch.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Gulch, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Friendly with us, and bandages when you are Honored.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.4,"n":"Kelm Hargunth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"8986":{"id":8986,"t":"More Components of Importance","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire Druidical Remains and return them to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\nDruidical Remains Hive'Regal Ambusher , Hive'Regal Burrower , Hive'Regal Spitfire , Hive'Regal Slavemaker and 1 more","desc":"‹class›, listen closely. Now that we have the location of the last amulet piece, we still need another component to suffuse the brazier with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.\nMor Grayhoof, our most prominent druid, had many close friends amongst the Cenarion Circle, some of which have fallen to the silithid. I need you to retrieve some Druidical Remains from the silithid that inhabit the environs of Hive'Regal in southeastern Silithus.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n3 Bloodkelp Elixir of Dodging 3 Bloodkelp Elixir of Resistance\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you returned already then, ‹class›, with what I sent you out to gather?","done":"A job well done, ‹name›. I will imbue the essence of the remains into the brazier.\nNow all that is left is to go to the lower portion of Blackrock Spire, to the chamber where War Master Voone resides in Tazz'Alaor, and use the brazier to summon forth the corrupted spirit of my former cohort, Mor Grayhoof. He cannot rest until the amulet piece is taken from him.\nOh, by the way, I had some leftover bloodkelp from your trip to Alcaz Isle, so I made it into some potions for you. Take your pick!\nBurning Steppes Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"5306":{"id":5306,"t":"Snakestone of the Shadow Huntress","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,550, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and slay Shadow Hunter Vosh'gajin. Recover Vosh'gajin's Snakestone and return to Kilram.\nVosh'gajin's Snakestone Shadow Hunter Vosh'gajin","desc":"Don't let her beauty fool you, ‹class›. The shadow huntress, Vosh'gajin is deadly and deranged.\n<Kilram points to the scar on his face.>\nAye, she gave me that - a love tap, she called it.\nThe time for vengeance has finally come.\nYou can find Vosh'gajin in Blackrock Spire. Slay her and return to me with her snakestone. Do this and I will teach you the secret to crafting Dawn's Edge!","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Dawn's Edge\nExperience: 8,300","back":"Legend states that one use of Vosh'gajin's snakestone will keep an axe razor sharp for a 1000 years!","done":"Knowledge is power!","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.3,"y":37.1,"n":"Kilram","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"2586":{"id":2586,"t":"Salt of the Scorpok","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring three Scorpok Pincers, two Vulture Gizzards, and one Blasted Boar Lung to Bloodmage Drazial.\n3 Scorpok Pincer Scorpok Stinger 40 % , Clack the Reaver 30 %\n2 Vulture Gizzard Black Slayer 40 % , Spiteflayer 30 %\nBlasted Boar Lung Ashmane Boar 40 % , Helboar 40 % , Grunter 30 %","desc":"You live! This is good news, indeed. I assume you are back for more of the scorpok assay?\nVery well, ‹name›, back to the wasteland with you and do not return until you have collected three scorpok pincers, two vulture gizzards, and one blasted boar lung.","rew":"You will receive:\nGround Scorpok Assay","back":"Where are the organs, ‹name›!?","done":"Fine work, ‹name›. Here is one sample of the assay for you and the remaining nine will be used in my research.\nAnytime you require more of the ground scorpok assay, return to me and we shall work out a deal.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":50.6,"y":14.2,"n":"Bloodmage Drazial","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"4186":{"id":4186,"t":"The True Masters","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Bolvar's Decree to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.\nBolvar's Decree\nProvided: Bolvar's Decree","desc":"I am going to empower you as an acting deputy of Stormwind, ‹name›.\nReturn to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire and deliver this decree.","rew":"Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Any news from Bolvar?","done":"It could have been worse, I suppose...\n<Magistrate Solomon looks you over.>\nIt appears as if the fate of Lakeshire rests squarely on your shoulders.\n<You notice Magistrate Solomon blinking rapidly. He appears to be crying.>\nStormwind City Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","e":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97946":{"id":97946,"t":"Camping 101 leatherworking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Nadyia Maneweaver on the road to Darnassus from Dolanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your leatherworking skill to 20","desc":"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, ‹class›. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","done":"There you have it, your very own camp tent. Most folk don't care much for tents being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":41.8,"y":49.4,"n":"Nadyia Maneweaver","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96986":{"id":96986,"t":"The grave knight","lv":33,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat Atrexis the Grave Knight in the City of Dalaran for Melisara in Tarren Mill.\nAtrexis the Grave Knight slain","desc":"Within the underbelly of the mage city to the north is a traitor to our kind. A necromancer of disturbing talent. He raises an army of undeath right under the Kirin Tor's nose.\nI care not for the fate of the mage city, ‹name›, but this grave knight spits in the face of everything we Forsaken stand for. Put an end to him. Show him no one is beyond the reach of the Dark Lady.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGravewalker Boots Undead Knight's Bracers\nMoney: 1 1 gold, 0 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,400","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.6,"y":20.6,"n":"Melisara","s":1}],"cats":["city-of-dalaran"]},"94266":{"id":94266,"t":"Craftsmans writ elixir of agility","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Elixir of Agility\nElixir of Agility","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Elixir of Agility, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Elixir of Agility Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94266","cats":["crafting"]},"94346":{"id":94346,"t":"Craftsmans writ runic leather headband","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Runic Leather Headband\nRunic Leather Headband","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Runic Leather Headband, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Runic Leather Headband Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94346","cats":["crafting"]},"7946":{"id":7946,"t":"Spawn of Jubjub","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Dark Iron Ale Mug Whit Wantmal , Dark Iron Ale Mug , Grim Guzzler Boar 4.1 % , Guzzling Patron 0.6 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nUnhatched Jubling Egg","back":"I'm so happy Jubjub is no longer lost. She loves Dark Iron ale so much that when I ran out... she ran away to find more!\nNow that Jubjub's back, I want as much ale as I can get! I won't want her to run away again!\nDo you have any Dark Iron Ale? If you do, then I'll trade you one of Jubjub's frog eggs for a mug...","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Here is your egg! It won't be ready to hatch for a little while, but when it does you'll have a great pet!\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.3,"y":70.3,"n":"Morja","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":36.9,"y":42.6,"n":"Morja","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"986":{"id":986,"t":"A Lost Master","lv":20,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find 5 Fine Moonstalker Pelts and return them to Terenthis in Auberdine.\n5 Fine Moonstalker Pelt Moonstalker Matriarch 40 % , Moonstalker Sire 40 %","desc":"‹name›, your skills have already helped me in my endeavor. Could I impose on you again to help Grimclaw and his master Volcor? In addition, I can craft you a magical cloak that will allow you to walk unhindered by Darkshore's creatures while you look for him.\nTo create the cloak, I'll need five fine moonstalker pelts from a moonstalker sire or matriarch to have enough material. The cats can be found near Wildbend River to the south, or even farther south near Ashenvale.","rew":"Experience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I can't in good conscience permit you to seek Volcor until I've crafted that cloak for you.","done":"These will do nicely, ‹name›. I shall set to work on the cloak immediately.\nGive me a few moments, then return to me.\nOh, one more thing: after you've used the enchantment on the cloak you'll be limited in your interactions with others. If you can help it, do no more than speak to others. Much more than that could dispel the illusion.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":39.4,"y":43.5,"n":"Terenthis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98906":{"id":98906,"t":"The battle for darkspear islands","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Win a Darkspear Islands battleground and return back to Nizook Boof at The Merchant Coast.\nWin in Darkspear Islands","desc":"The battle at the Darkspear Islands be locked in a stalemate, ‹class›. Show those Alliance fools who the superior force is.\nCarry your head high in service of the Darkspear and claim victory in battle. The Loa will surely be givin' you their blessing, ‹class›!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000\n+200 reputation with Darkspear Raiders","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":65,"y":34.8,"n":"Nizook Boof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"1386":{"id":1386,"t":"Assault on the Kolkar","lv":32,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram. Kill 12 Kolkar Centaurs, 12 Kolkar Scouts and 6 Kolkar Maulers, then return to Warug in the Magram Village in Desolace.\nKolkar Centaur slain : 0/ 12\nKolkar Scout slain : 0/ 12\nKolkar Mauler slain : 0/ 6\nReach 3000 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur","desc":"The Kolkar think they are strong, but we laugh at them! We laugh and we kill them! You kill them too. Show me you can kill Kolkar like we do. Head north and slay them all!","rew":"Experience: 2,550","back":"Are you afraid of the Kolkar? Why do you not kill them? Maybe you forgot how to kill. Hurry and kill Kolkar before they are dead!","done":"The Kolkar fear you now! I hope you laughed when you killed them. It is better to laugh when you kill, so the enemy can see he is weak.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":75,"y":68.2,"n":"Warug","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5386":{"id":5386,"t":"Catch of the Day","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Jinar'Zillen at Shadowprey Village, and then bring Nataka Longhorn 2 Bloodbelly fish.\n2 Bloodbelly Fish","desc":"The smell of cooked fish has long been missing here at Ghost Walker Post. The trolls at Shadowprey Village are the best at catching fish... but alas, with all the centaur activities I have little time to make a journey to the trolls. Hrm...\nDo me a favor and journey to Shadowprey Village. Talk to the local fisherman Jinar'Zillen and bring me back my favorite, Bloodbelly fish. The road south of here will take you west to the troll village.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n3 Mithril Ore 5 Thick Leather 5 Mageweave Cloth\nExperience: 2,100\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"My hoof tingles and my mouth starts to water when I think of fried Bloodbelly fish... You have any on you?","done":"You are a savior, ‹name›! These Bloodbelly fish look almost good enough to eat raw.\n<Nataka starts salivating.>\nHere you go - choose one of these items as a payment for these fish.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":55.4,"y":55.8,"n":"Nataka Longhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"1466":{"id":1466,"t":"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc.","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Felhound Brains, 10 Nether Wings, and 10 vials of Doomwarder Blood to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.\n10 Felhound Brain Mana Eater 80 % , Mage Hunter 80 % , Ley Hunter 80 %\n10 Nether Wing Nether Sorceress 80 % , Nether Sister 80 % , Nether Maiden 80 %\n10 Doomwarder Blood Lord Azrethoc 80 % , Doomwarder Captain 80 % , Kaskk 80 %","desc":"This is the last of the items, and I won't lie, it ain't pretty. I'm also expecting this to take you a little bit longer than the other items.\nSo, enough with the warning, let's get this started. Leftwitch says he needs: ten brains from either mana eaters, mage hunters, or ley hunters. Ten nether wings from a nether maiden, sister or sorceress. And... ten vials of doomwarder blood from a doomwarder captain, or lord.\nSimple enough, huh? Sheesh... if you wanna pass on this one, I'd understand.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I didn't even realize these demon things were in Desolace. Last I read, centaur pretty much owned the land after the night elves picked up and left years ago.\nI wonder why they took up here, and how.","done":"Honestly? I wouldn't have thought it. You're amazing, ‹name›. Taking on demons for a mage's experiments, and coming back in one piece to boot. Great job!\nI'm personally gonna tell Roetten about you when I get back to Ironforge.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.2,"y":9.6,"n":"Kreldig Ungor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"93226":{"id":93226,"t":"Buying friendship magram","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Totem Tote to the Magram Quartermaster at Magram Village in the Desolace to significantly increase your reputation with that clan. You must be of at least Neutral standing with the Magram Clan Centaur.\nProvided: Totem Tote","desc":"Siding with the Magram would be my choice. There is no question that they are the dominant clan in the present day, regardless of their previous struggles. I have heard reports that they are brutally hostile against the Gelkis.\nI sympathize with both warring clans and especially the Gelkis, but this is their war; not ours. We ought to side with the faction that poses the least risk to our cause. I believe that to be the Magram.\nBring this to their quartermaster in Magram Village to the southeast.\nLevel 45 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 41 43 48 57 Side Both factions Quest ID 93226","cats":["desolace"]},"26":{"id":26,"t":"A Lesson to Learn","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.","desc":"‹name›, I have been following your progress with much delight. You are most assuredly developing yourself into a valued protector of nature.\nThe time has come for you to learn more about one of the various animal aspects that Cenarius has blessed us with the ability to change into - one that affords you command and mastery of the water. For this, you must travel to the village of Nighthaven in Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle there. He will guide you further.","rew":"Experience: 120","done":"Salutations, young ‹class›; the time has come for you to know our aquatic form. It is one that lets you move freely and indefinitely through water. You will find this aspect a useful tool and a blessing... but it is one that must be earned before it is mastered.\nYou will face two trials to overcome. The first will test your ability to work in water under pressure. The second will test your resolve to understand the aspects of the form itself.\nStand ready, as the time of testing is now upon us.\nThunder Bluff Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Turak Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"826":{"id":826,"t":"Zalazane","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat Zalazane.\nKill 8 Voodoo Trolls and 8 Hexed Trolls.\nBring Zalazane's Head to Gadrin.\nZalazane's Head Zalazane\nHexed Troll slain : 0/ 8\nVoodoo Troll slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The witchdoctor Zalazane dwells on the Echo Isles to the east. They are the isles we once called home.\nFrom there he sends his trolls to the mainland, to hex our people and drag more of them under his sway.\nHe must be stopped.\nDefeat Zalazane and his minions -- former Darkspear trolls, now lost to us. Bring me his head and I will know his reign of evil is over.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLightweight Boots Veiled Grips\nExperience: 850\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Is Zalazane defeated, ‹name›?","done":"With Zalazane gone, our tribe can again sleep in peace.\nThank you, ‹name›. The Darkspear tribe owes you much. If you suffer from an ailment, visit my assistant Bom'bay, behind me. His voodoo is strong...","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.9,"y":74.7,"n":"Master Gadrin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"266":{"id":266,"t":"Inquire at the Inn","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search the inn for clues about the shadowy figure.\nBook from Sven's Farm\nProvided: Book from Sven's Farm","desc":"Here is your book, and good luck with your inquiries.\nYou might want to expand your search to the inn. If the person whom you seek spent time in town, then chances are someone saw him there.","rew":"Experience: 200","back":"The Scarlet Raven doesn't see the business it used to, but we still do get travelers passing through.\nIf you can describe the person you're looking for, maybe I'll remember him.","done":"Oh yeah, I remember this book. Its owner rented a room for a few days, and spent his nights at the bar, writing.\nHe left town in a hurry, muttering about being hunted by...something. Last I saw him he was heading west out of town, looking for a new spot to hide.\nThe first place he'd find to the west is Raven Hill...","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.5,"y":46.9,"n":"Clerk Daltry","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Tavernkeep Smitts","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"6026":{"id":6026,"t":"That's Asking A Lot","lv":58,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Smokey LaRue wants you to get 2 Thorium Bars, 1 Golden Rod, 8 Hi-Explosive Bombs, and 8 Unstable Triggers.\nYou will have to find a blacksmith and an engineer for these items.\n2 Thorium Bar\nGolden Rod\n8 Hi-Explosive Bomb\n8 Unstable Trigger","desc":"These here Argent Dawn people commissioned ol' Smokey to do a little demolition work for 'em. Smokey's mammy ain't raised no dummy. When gold coin is slapped on the table, Smokey's services are available. That's my motto!\nNow I'd be willing to split the commission with you if you're willing to do a little legwork. Here's the deal: I'm going to head over to Plaguewood and mark the buildings we need destroyed. You gather the components for the bombs. Meet back here when you've got everything. Deal?","rew":"Money: 1 75 1 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200","back":"Trust ol' Smokey, ‹race›. The reward will be worth it. These Argent Dawn folk don't mess around when it comes to payment.","done":"I can pay you half up front and half when the job is done.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.9,"y":48.4,"n":"Smokey LaRue","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9226":{"id":9226,"t":"Superior Armaments of Battle - Revered Amongst the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"For 7 Insignias of the Dawn and 7 Insignias of the Crusade you may choose an item from the Argent Dawn's treasure cache.\n7 Insignia of the Dawn\n7 Insignia of the Crusade","desc":"Greetings, friend. Have you insignias of the Dawn or the Crusade that you would like to redeem for items of power?\nItems offered to those revered amongst the Dawn are priced quite reasonably. I encourage you to make a purchase!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBand of Piety Band of Resolution Verimonde's Last Resort Supply Bag Leggings of the Plague Hunter Sanctified Leather Helm\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Choose carefully. There are no refunds.","done":"Good day, ‹name›. It was a pleasure doing business with you.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.8,"y":50.2,"n":"Quartermaster Miranda Breechlock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"106":{"id":106,"t":"Young Lovers","lv":6,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Maybell's Love Letter to Tommy Joe Stonefield.\nMaybell's Love Letter\nProvided: Maybell's Love Letter","desc":"Oh, I'm cursed! My heart belongs to Tommy Joe Stonefield, but our families are bitter enemies. So I can't see him, even though my eyes ache to gaze upon that handsome face!\nPlease, take this letter and give it to Tommy Joe. He's usually at the river to the west of the Stonefield Farm, which is due west of here.","rew":"Experience: 140\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have what?? Maybell is the light of my dull life. Hurry, let me see her letter!","done":"Ah! I can't stand us being apart. I have to see her!!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.2,"y":89.6,"n":"Maybell Maclure","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":29.8,"y":86,"n":"Tommy Joe Stonefield","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"4506":{"id":4506,"t":"Corrupted Sabers","lv":54,"min":49,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Winna's kitten to the corrupted moonwell, release it, then bring it back to Winna.\nOnce you have returned to Winna, click on the cat to release it to Winna.\nProvided: Winna's Kitten Carrier","desc":"This corrupted water can be used to our advantage, ‹name›. With just a small amount of the water, my kitten doubled in size, and seems to be stronger... somehow. These cats may prove useful...\nHere, ‹name›. Take this cat carrier, and release the kitten inside next to the moonwell in the Ruins of Constellas. Heh, heh... I'm sure you'll be pleased with the results!\nReturn the cat to me, and I'm sure I can make it worth your time.","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Don't tell me that you can't go back there! Get going!","done":"Excellent!\nThe forsaken will resort to any means necessary to crush the alliance! The use of the corrupted water will surely prove useful in our future efforts...","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.2,"y":52.3,"n":"Winna Hazzard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4906":{"id":4906,"t":"Further Corruption","lv":54,"min":49,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Eridan Bluewind in Felwood wants you to kill 8 Jadefire Hellcallers, 8 Jadefire Betrayers, 8 Jadefire Tricksters, and Xavaric. Return to Eridan when the task is completed.\nJadefire Hellcaller slain : 0/ 8\nJadefire Betrayer slain : 0/ 8\nJadefire Trickster slain : 0/ 8\nXavaric slain","desc":"A second encampment of satyrs threatens the land of Felwood towards the north, led by the cruel Xavaric. The vile betrayers and tricksters feed upon the corruption of the native creatures of Felwood.\nXavathras and his minions were only part of a larger plan -- to cultivate a corrupted moonwell, and then provide the spoils to Xavaric.\nNow that Xavathras is out of the way, finish this task, ‹name›. Head to the north and defeat Xavaric.","rew":"You will receive:\nBreezecloud Bracers\nExperience: 5,450","back":"Please, put and end to the suffering of Felwood's creatures.","done":"Thank you for all you have done, ‹name›. May Elune protect you and guide you on the path ahead.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":81.5,"n":"Eridan Bluewind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4106":{"id":4106,"t":"Salve via Skinning","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Patch of Tainted Skin","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"A Cenarion beacon will allow a well-trained skinner to spot patches of tainted skin from bounty gathered in Felwood. I convert these seemingly useless patches into a thick paste that serves as a quickening agent for Cenarion plant salve. When you skin your kills here in Felwood, be sure to have a beacon on you!\nWhen you collect tainted patches, bring them to me and I will give you some Cenarion plant salves that I have already made.","done":"This is exactly what I need. Here - take these plant salves and use them to reclaim Felwood from the corruption. We must persevere, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4266":{"id":4266,"t":"A Hero's Welcome","lv":46,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Shandris Feathermoon in Feathermoon Stronghold.","desc":"‹name›, General Shandris Feathermoon would like to speak with you personally. No doubt she wants to thank you for your service to the Stronghold, but I do know that she also wants to talk to you about the insect creatures that you and Raschal faced in southern Feralas. The reports of those Zukk'ash insects are... frightening, to say the least.\nGeneral Feathermoon is waiting for you in the main compound.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCeremonial Elven Blade Sanctimonial Rod\nExperience: 6,050\n+200 reputation with Alliance","done":"‹name›, I give you my warmest thanks for the aid you've given us. Your bravery in the face of overwhelming odds has warranted a reward worth a thousand times greater. Nevertheless, I hope you accept this on behalf of the entire Stronghold.\nNow, if I may... I'd like to ask for your aid one more time. In light of the discovery of the Zukk'ash hive here in Feralas, I think you're the best choice for this mission.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":31.9,"y":45.1,"n":"Ginro Hearthkindle","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":30.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Shandris Feathermoon","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"97066":{"id":97066,"t":"Tip the scales brownells blue striped racer","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Brownell's Blue Striped Racer","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Speckled Tastyfish\nLevel 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 97066","cats":["fishing"]},"506":{"id":506,"t":"Blackmoore's Legacy","lv":36,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the information gathered by Gol'dir to Krusk in Tarren Mill.","desc":"A day or two ago, I was visited by the leader of this Syndicate. His name was Aliden Perenolde, and styled himself lord of this land. He confided in me his plans to take the orcs that stood against him as slaves, just as his father and his mentor, the despised Blackmoore, had planned.\nMore important was that he brought his mistress, a wisp of a girl named Elysa. Around her neck was the pendant the Warchief desires.\nNow go, I will make my own way, after I have settled my business here.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"The nerve of those overbearing humans! We'll show them that the orcs shall never submit to their will!\nThis will now be our mission, in addition to recovering the trinket the Warchief desires. It would seem that by accomplishing one, we will also accomplish the other.\nAlterac Mountains Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":60,"y":43.7,"n":"Gol'dir","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":63.2,"y":20.7,"n":"Krusk","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"8906":{"id":8906,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Beaststalker's Bindings to Deliana in Ironforge.\n15 Winterspring Blood Sample Rabid Shardtooth 30 % , Elder Shardtooth 30 % , Shardtooth Bear 30 % , Shardtooth Mauler 30 % and 4 more\nBeaststalker's Bindings Fleshflayer Ghoul 4.3 % in Stratholme , Ghoul Ravener 4 % in Stratholme , Crimson Defender 2 % in Stratholme , Rage Talon Dragonspawn 1.7 %","desc":"Well met, ‹class›. I've something that might interest you.\nI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality. I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.\nThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment. Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold. You shall find the effort worth your while.","rew":"You will receive:\nBeastmaster's Bindings\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you brought me what I requested of you, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent! Let's perform the trade then. It's hard to part with this excellent armor, but I'm afraid I won't be needing it any time soon.\nIf you're interested in performing more work for me, I might be willing to give up the rest of the pieces.\nDun Morogh Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"5146":{"id":5146,"t":"Elemental Leatherworking","lv":55,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Heart of Fire, 2 Globe of Water, 2 Core of Earth, and 2 Breath of Wind to Brumn Winterhoof in the Arathi Mountains.\nCompleting this quest will give you access to the Elemental Leatherworking arts.\nThe completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Dragonscale Leatherworking and Tribal Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.\n2 Heart of Fire Baron Charr 69.9 % , Prince Skaldrenox 41.7 % , Golemagg the Incinerator 30 % , Baron Geddon 30 % and 4 more\n2 Globe of Water Princess Tempestria 77.1 % , Lord Skwol 47.6 % , Hydrospawn 20 % , Muck Splash 16.1 % and 4 more\n2 Core of Earth Avalanchion 78.6 % , Baron Kazum 57.4 % , Golemagg the Incinerator 30 % , Garr 30 % and 4 more\n2 Breath of Wind Gusting Vortex 83.8 % , The Windreaver 76 % , Living Storm 66.7 % , High Marshal Whirlaxis 35.9 % and 4 more","desc":"Elemental leatherworking is what I know, and if you're willing to open your mind to the greater powers of substance, I will share with you all there is to learn.\nKnow this, ‹class›: by choosing this path you agree never to learn dragonscale or tribal leatherworking; there is only room for practice of one of the three arts. Furthermore, I'll need adequate proof that you are in tune with the elements of nature; to that end, bring me the purest essences of fire, water, earth, and wind.","rew":"You will learn: Elemental Leatherworking\nExperience: 4,200\n+200 reputation with Leatherworking - Elemental","back":"Making this kind of leather-based armor requires patience and dedication. Once you have cast your lot with the elements, there is no turning your back on them. Bring me proof of your worthiness, and we'll get started.","done":"You've cast your lot, and the elements accept you. Once I have finished my tutelage, you shall command the will to craft the finest of leather garbs.\nTo train in the art for the future, simply speak to me and I will make available any knowledge that you have yet to commit as yours.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":28.3,"y":45.1,"n":"Brumn Winterhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"7786":{"id":7786,"t":"Thunderaan the Windseeker","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 10,900, 0.91 times as much.","obj":"To free Thunderaan the Windseeker from his prison, you must present the right and left halves of the Bindings of the Windseeker, 10 bars of Elementium, and the Essence of the Firelord to Highlord Demitrian in Silithus.\n10 Elementium Bar\nEssence of the Firelord Ragnaros\nBindings of the Windseeker Baron Geddon 4 %\nBindings of the Windseeker Garr 4 %","desc":"I have told you all that I know, ‹name›. It is you who must find elementium. It is you who must destroy the Firelord's corporeal form.\nDo this and gain the blessing of Thunderaan.","rew":"Experience: 9,950","back":"Bring the world to its knees if you must!","done":"Even in dreams I did not dare foresee this day.\nBehold, mortal.\nBEHOLD HE WHO IS OLDER THAN EXISTENCE!\nBEHOLD HE WHO HAS FACED TITAN AND GOD ALIKE!\nRISE MY MASTER! BREAK FROM YOUR BONDS!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":21.7,"y":8.6,"n":"Highlord Demitrian","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["legendary"]},"1946":{"id":1946,"t":"Nether-lace Garment","lv":26,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nNether-lace Robe Nether-lace Tunic\nExperience: 2,100","done":"Here is your nether-lace, ‹name›. It is both comfortable and durable, and holds the magic of the laughing sisters' hair.\nEnjoy, and if you find it amenable, please mention so to Deino. She is a mage on whose good side I wish to stay...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.2,"y":31.7,"n":"Kil'hala","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"7066":{"id":7066,"t":"Seed of Life","lv":51,"min":39,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 39 instead of 45.","obj":"Seek out Remulos in Moonglade and give him the Seed of Life.\nSeed of Life\nProvided: Seed of Life","desc":"The misbegotten centaur--my sons and daughters--have need of their father.\nLook around you--this place rings of hope and all that my father Cenarius preaches. It sprung from me! And I cannot take that away from them... not even for their crimes against me.\nBut there is one thing I would ask of you to ease my brother's mind. Take this... it is the first seed that fell from the life my remains nourished. Tell him my spirit remains here, and that I live on. I am sure he will understand.","rew":"Money: 1 50 1 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,100\n+150 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have the scent of corruption on you, ‹name›... much like many adventurers these days. But something about you is different. Is there something you've come to speak to me about? You have an aura about you that seems familiar, but I cannot place it.\nPlease, I implore you, tell me why you've sought an audience with me.","done":"So my brother has finally found peace? I am proud to have lived to see this day. In all his arrogance and anger, I truly thought he was lost to us, but this... this symbol of his sacrifice only proves that he is not lost--he has only been reborn. He takes his place in nature as was his duty.\nThank you, ‹name›. By bringing this to me, you have secured a small amount of hope that I thought I had once lost. This seed will be important to the people of this war-torn land some day... I can sense it.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.2,"y":41.8,"n":"Keeper Remulos","e":1}],"cats":["maraudon"]},"9386":{"id":9386,"t":"A Light in Dark Places","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. No longer rewards Captured Flame.","obj":"Find and touch the bonfires located within Blackrock Spire, Dire Maul, Scholomance, and Stratholme, then speak with the Festival Flamekeeper.\nFlame of Dire Maul\nFlame of Blackrock Spire\nFlame of Stratholme in Stratholme\nFlame of the Scholomance in Scholomance","desc":"An eager one, aren't you? If you're willing to enter the depths once more, I'll gladly reward you.\nSeek out the bonfires burning within Stratholme, Scholomance, Dire Maul, and the halls of Blackrock Spire itself; I look forward to your return, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Burning Blossom","back":"Have you found your way through the dark?","done":"You have proven that you are not entirely useless, mortal.\nOrgrimmar Tirisfal Glades Teldrassil Silverpine Forest Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.6,"y":34.2,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.6,"y":91.9,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"746":{"id":746,"t":"Dwarven Digging","lv":8,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 5 Prospector's Picks.\nAt a forge, smash the Prospector's Picks to create Broken Tools.\nBring 5 Broken Tools to Baine Bloodhoof in Bloodhoof Village.\n5 Broken Tools","desc":"There are dwarves preparing a dig site to the northwest. They think secrets lie in the earth, and that is true, but hollowing and defiling the land is no way to earn its teachings.\nCollect the dwarven tools of digging, smash them, and return to me with the dwarves' broken tools.\nYou can smash the tools at a forge. You will find one in Thunder Bluff, but any forge -- even a forge at the dwarven camp -- will suffice.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFortified Bindings Rough-hewn Kodo Leggings\nExperience: 700\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Do you have the Broken Tools? The dwarves' digging will enrage the kodos of Mulgore. This defilement must be stopped!","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. This will calm the beasts of Mulgore. And, spirits willing, it will teach the dwarves that hollowing the land is not the path to knowledge.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.7,"y":63.4,"n":"Baine Bloodhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"1146":{"id":1146,"t":"The Swarm Grows","lv":33,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Belgrom's Sealed Note to Moktar Krin in Thousand Needles.\nBelgrom's Sealed Note\nProvided: Belgrom's Sealed Note","desc":"So, Korran has come to a similar conclusion about these insects--they seem to be a larger threat than we assumed.\nA few days ago a hunter returned to me from Thousand Needles nearly dead. He was with a raiding party sent to drive a dwarven excavation team out of the Shimmering Flats. During the attack, more of these insects erupted from a cave in the dig site and nearly killed the party.\nThey were led by Moktar Krin, and they've taken refuge on the border of the Shimmering Flats. Bring him this note.","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"War brings my group and I to the Shimmering Flats, ‹class›. What brings you here?","done":"Don't mind the thundering echoes off the mountains' walls. The goblins and gnomes are out among the Flats racing one another in atrocities created by what they call science. There are bigger threats here in Thousand Needles, one of which killed more than half my war party.\nBut we remain here until we hear word from Belgrom in Orgrimmar. Until then, we hold our position here, and stay vigilant.\nOrgrimmar Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":75.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Belgrom Rockmaul","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":67.6,"y":63.9,"n":"Moktar Krin","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1786":{"id":1786,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Symbol of Life and resurrect Henze Faulk in Elwynn.\nHenze Faulk","desc":"Henze and I had made it to Heroes' Vigil, an island in the middle of Stone Cairn Lake in northeastern Elwynn. We'd heard the Defias had infiltrated our borders and we wanted proof to take to the king's advisors.\nWe caught sight of a couple of the scum going over some documents, and we attacked. Unfortunately, we were quickly overwhelmed by more of the mages.\nHenze held them off for me while I escaped... the daft fool, going and being brave.\nHe's out there now, Henze is. Can you help us, ‹name›?","rew":"Experience: 675","done":"Thank you, brother/sister.\nSeeing you wield the Symbol of Life, may I assume Duthorian or Gazin sent you?\nI fell to the Defias spell casters while Gazin and I tried to get their plans from them: I was able to hold on long enough to allow Gazin to escape, but in the end, their magics overwhelmed me.\nBut you were able to bring me back: the ability to use the Symbol doesn't come to just anyone, ‹name›. It bodes well for you that you were able to empower it with your own faith.\nStormwind City Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":45,"n":"Gazin Tenorm","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":72.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Henze Faulk","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5626":{"id":5626,"t":"In Favor of the Light","lv":4,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Maxan Anvol in Dun Morogh.","desc":"Hey! ‹name›! Got a minute?!\nYa been following the Light now for long enough that you find your way to Maxan Anvol in Kharanos. He'll teach ya more about the path yer following, and if you prove worthy, give ya yer first set of robes to denote your station as a priest/priestess.\nNow get goin'! As soon as yer done here, head through the tunnel--he'll be waitin' for ya.","rew":"Experience: 90","done":"Oh, so Branstock sent ya, did he? Good, good! He's right, it is 'bout time you started taking a much larger step into the Light. It'll build character and make ya stronger... an' that's what you'll need more than anything: strength of body... strength of will.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.6,"y":66.4,"n":"Branstock Khalder","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.3,"y":52.2,"n":"Maxan Anvol","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"94826":{"id":94826,"t":"Confounding flash","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.","desc":"Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, ‹name›.\nAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.\nWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out your High Priestess for further training.\nLevel 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Alliance Class Priest Shareable Yes Quest ID 94826","cats":["priest"]},"8826":{"id":8826,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Horde Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with the Darkspear tribe. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":30.4,"y":65.6,"n":"Undercity Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":46.3,"y":35.1,"n":"Officer Vu'Shalay","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"5466":{"id":5466,"t":"The Lich, Ras Frostwhisper","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Ras Frostwhisper in the Scholomance. When you have found him, use the Soulbound Keepsake on his undead visage. Should you succeed in reverting him to a mortal, strike him down and recover the Human Head of Ras Frostwhisper. Take the head back to Magistrate Marduke.\nHuman Head of Ras Frostwhisper Ras Frostwhisper in Scholomance\nProvided: Soulbound Keepsake","desc":"There is but one task remaining, ‹name›. Confront the lich, Ras Frostwhisper, in his lair.\nUse the power of the keepsake against the beast - be unrelenting in your actions! Weather the blows that the flailing beast will surely bring down upon you. Do not give in to the pain!\nWhen the ritual is complete, Ras will be mortal once more. It is at that point that he must be slain. Strike him down and take his human head.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWarblade of Caer Darrow Crown of Caer Darrow Darrowspike\nYou will also receive:\nDarrowshire Strongguard\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You carry the burden of ten thousand restless souls, ‹name›.","done":"Ten thousand souls cry out in unison, ‹name›! You have struck a mortal blow to the Scourge and their masters.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":70.6,"y":74.1,"n":"Magistrate Marduke","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"8746":{"id":8746,"t":"Metzen the Reindeer","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Metzen the Reindeer. Use the notes provided to you for clues as to where he is being held.\nWhen you find Metzen, have the Pouch of Reindeer Dust in your possession so you can sprinkle some of the dust on him; this should free Metzen from his bonds of captivity.\nReturn the Pouch of Reindeer Dust to Kaymard Copperpinch in Orgrimmar once Metzen is freed.\nPouch of Reindeer Dust Eldreth Spirit , Southsea Pirate , Shadowforge Digger , Glassweb Spider and 1 more\nFind Metzen the Reindeer and rescue him\nProvided: Smokywood Satchel","desc":"DISASTER has struck! Metzen the Reindeer has been kidnapped!\nMetzen is one of Great-father Winter's eight reindeer - and property of Smokywood Pastures. We've received not one but TWO ransom letters from groups claiming to have Metzen. With the holiday season well under way, we're strapped to the coin box here! Please - find Metzen and return him to us!\nCheck out the ransom letters for clues, and sprinkle this reindeer dust on him - it will free him from any of his bonds!\nPlease, hurry!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Preserved Holly\nExperience: 4,950\n+200 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"‹name›! Did you find him? Were the notes in the satchel I gave you enough information to locate Metzen? I hate to think of what those cruel thugs might do to him... but there's no way we can afford to pay such an exorbitant ransom!","done":"You did it! Huzzah!\nMetzen flew back into Great-father Winter's stables - yes Metzen can really fly - just a little while ago! The dust worked like a charm; I knew it would. You've saved the Feast of Winter Veil as well as Smokywood Pastures from disaster. Thank you, ‹name›.\nListen... because of what you've done here, I want you to have this. It's something VERY special; if you have a mount, I think you'll get a kick out of it. Happy Winter Veil!\nOrgrimmar Searing Gorge Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":53.3,"y":66.5,"n":"Kaymard Copperpinch","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"2986":{"id":2986,"t":"Call of Water","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.","desc":"Long has it been since you were last tested, ‹name›. You have shown patience thus far in your studies, but the time has come for you to learn more. The time has come for you to learn about the purity of water.\nSeek out Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. She is along the eastern coast, south of the Southfury River and Ratchet. You will find her there at her fishing hut. Good luck to you, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 775","done":"The wind approaches you quickly from the horizon; the earth is steady beneath your feet; and your spirit is already warmed by fire--I would say it is time for you to learn about the purity of water.\nYour path has led you this far, and your spirit will give you the strength to carry on even further. But the first step is yours to take.\nMulgore The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.4,"y":62.5,"n":"Narm Skychaser","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"93066":{"id":93066,"t":"Bristleback retreat","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay quilboar at Bristleback Retreat. Then report to Hagiak at the Magram Front on the other side of Valley of Bones in Desolace.\nBristleback Nomad slain : 0/ 4\nBristleback Thornweaver slain : 0/ 6\nBristleback Skullcrusher slain : 0/ 6\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"On the other side of the valley, we have established a small foothold to prepare to march into the forest nearby. Before you head straight there, I want you to deal with a recent Bristleback intrusion along the way. They seem to have arrived right around the same time we did, but managed to secure an artifact from the nearby temple that has kept us at bay.\nThis task is simple. Look for the thorns and the pigs. Kill a bunch, indiscriminately. Then report to Hagiak at the camp I mentioned.","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,600\n+500 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\nLevel 43 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 39 41 46 54 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93066\nThe chain\n15 quests from level 32 to 43, 36,630 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 40 ] Bone Raising\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones.\n2,350 XP\n[ 42 ] No Mercy for the Weak\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay 5 Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n10 [ 43 ] Bristleback Retreat this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay quilboar at Bristleback Retreat.\n3,600 XP\n11 [ 43 ] Long-Term Solutions\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram clan and slay 2 Outcast Scouts, 6 Outcast Marauders, and 8 Outcast Necromancers then return to Hagiak","cats":["shendralas"]},"346":{"id":346,"t":"Return to Kristoff","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Brother Kristoff in the Cathedral Square. Give him the book The Stresses of Iron.\nBook: Stresses of Iron\nProvided: Book: Stresses of Iron","desc":"Now that I've finished copying the book, here's the original Stresses of Iron. Thank you for your patience, and if you see Milton please tell him I'm sorry for the long delay.","rew":"You will receive:\nWandering Boots\nExperience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Were you able to find the book?","done":"That's the one! Thank you, ‹name›. May the Light shine brightly upon both your body and spirit!\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.6,"y":40.4,"n":"Brother Paxton","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":55,"y":54.2,"n":"Brother Kristoff","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"2746":{"id":2746,"t":"Items of Some Consequence","lv":31,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Silk Cloth and 2 of Clara's Fresh Apples to Tyrion in Stormwind.\n3 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more\n2 Clara's Fresh Apple Clara's Fresh Apples","desc":"Trias wants the timetable pushed up some, huh? Okay, we can do that, but I'm not ready. And know this, I'm doing the hard part, but you're the one that's going to get his/her hands dirty, understand? Good.\nOkay, I'll need you to get me a few things before I can put my plan into effect. I got the perfect disguise that'll get Spybot past those guards.\nBring me some silk and a couple apples. The silk's up to you, but Clara's little farm right outside the city has the perfect sized apples.","rew":"Experience: 625\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I've been watching Lescovar for a couple weeks now. Trias has never trusted him, but we didn't suspect he was involved in anything to do with the Defias Brotherhood. We were following leads that tied him to the Twilight's Hammer. Either way, he's become more dangerous than this city can deal with, and that's where we come in.\nGet me those items and we can put my plan into effect.","done":"These will do nicely, ‹name›. Great job.\nI have the rest of the gear I'll need in my pack... thank the Light I just got a tailor friend of mine to make me a silk bag. I was running out of room carrying all my gear around.\nBefore Spybot heads in, let's get the details set so you know what you have to do.\nStormwind City Elwynn Forest Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":73.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tyrion","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"5066":{"id":5066,"t":"A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!","lv":50,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist. His base camp is located at Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains.","desc":"Hear ye, hear ye! All heroes are called upon to heed these words!\nA call to arms has been issued by the Kingdom of Stormwind! All able bodied individuals are entreated to take up arms against the dark threat of the Scourge in the northern lands of the Eastern Kingdoms! Rumors fly of new threats rising from the ruins of the Plaguelands!\nHeroes of the realm - seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist who has set up his base camp in Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains!","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Welcome to the Plaguelands, hero. This is one of most dangerous frontiers in Azeroth, especially with the looming threat of the Scourge to our north and northeast. I am glad to hear that the clarion call of duty and service to the greater good did not fall on deaf ears with you!\nIf you are ready to get your hands dirty, then there is plenty for willing and able heroes to do here on the edge of the Plaguelands.\nStormwind City Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":56.4,"y":74.1,"n":"Crier Goodman","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"6186":{"id":6186,"t":"The Blightcaller Cometh","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Stormwind and inform Highlord Bolvar Fordragon of the fate of Nathanos Marris.","desc":"<The blood appears to have completely drained from Flint's face.>\nNa... Nathanos did this? Nathanos is the Blightcaller?\nWhy? He was... was so noble - a ranger lord respected by all. The only human ever allowed to train under the high elves. Now a ruthless agent of the Forsaken?\nI... I am sorry to ask this of you, ‹name›, but Highlord Fordragon must be informed of this turn of events at once. Please, return to Stormwind and deliver the news.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","done":"No. It... NO! How? An agent of the Forsaken? The CHAMPION of the Banshee Queen???\n<Highlord Bolvar Fordragon slumps in defeat.>\nWestern Plaguelands Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43.6,"y":84.5,"n":"Flint Shadowmore","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"186":{"id":186,"t":"Tiger Mastery","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ajeck Rouack of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Stranglethorn Tigers.\nStranglethorn Tiger slain : 0/ 10","desc":"You are learning, ‹class›. Let us test your skills with the mature cats now. Kill 10 Stranglethorn Tigers this time out.","rew":"Experience: 1,300","back":"If you strive for greater challenges you must first prove yourself with the task at hand. Return to me after you've killed 10 Stranglethorn Tigers.","done":"I am impressed, ‹class›. You are progressing quite well.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.6,"y":10.6,"n":"Ajeck Rouack","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"586":{"id":586,"t":"Speaking with Gan'zulah","lv":46,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Skullsplitter Hunters, 6 Skullsplitter Headhunters, and 4 Skullsplitter Berserkers.\nBring the Broken Armor of Ana'thek to the Bubbling Cauldron at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\nBroken Armor of Ana'thek Ana'thek the Cruel\nSkullsplitter Hunter slain : 0/ 8\nSkullsplitter Headhunter slain : 0/ 6\nSkullsplitter Berserker slain : 0/ 4","desc":"<The head of Gan'zulah speaks.>\nCurse you! And curse your ancestors!!\nOnly blood and revenge can cool my rage, so if that is your wish, then... do this:\nThrow yourself into the heart of the Skullsplitters to the east. Slay the fiercest among them, and if you survive...then break yourself against their chief, Ana'thek the Cruel. Hah! Bring me his shattered armor if you can!\nMay he tear off your limbs and leave you to rot and be eaten by carrion.","rew":"Experience: 4,050\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Although my own flesh boils off my skull, I can still smell your fear.\nHah! You will never complete my task...","done":"I do not want to believe it, but I cannot deny what you have done. And my rage eases, now that Ana'thek is defeated.\nYour might will drive you to great deeds, ‹name›. But one day...I will see you in the Nether and we will again match strength.\nI will be waiting.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.6,"n":"Bubbling Cauldron","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3626":{"id":3626,"t":"Return to the Blasted Lands","lv":58,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.","desc":"The hour of redemption is near, ‹name›. You must return to the Blasted Lands with your new-found weaponry and speak with the Fallen Hero of the Horde to receive your final objective.","rew":"Experience: 1,550","done":"You look battle hardened, ‹name›. Are you prepared to face Razelikh and his minions?\nStranglethorn Vale Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":50.6,"y":20.5,"n":"Galvan the Ancient","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8586":{"id":8586,"t":"Dirge's Kickin' Chimaerok Chops","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Dirge Quikcleave in Gadgetzan wants you to bring him 20 Goblin Rocket Fuel and 20 Deeprock Salt.\n20 Goblin Rocket Fuel Stormpike Shredder Unit 19 % , 7:XT 2.3 % , Clunk 1.2 % , Tortured Druid 0 % and 2 more\n20 Deeprock Salt Garr 30 % , Setis 24.5 % , Infernal Bodyguard 24.1 % , Faulty War Golem 24 % and 4 more","desc":"My recipe is complete! What I need from you now is some rocket fuel and deeprock salt. I'll handle the spices and the meat you brought me will cover the rest.\nAfter you bring me what I asked for, the chicken will be ready to take back to Narain.","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Dirge's Kickin' Chimaerok Chops 20 Dirge's Kickin' Chimaerok Chops\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Hurry it up, kid. We don't want this meat to go bad.","done":"It's ready! I present to you my greatest creation: Dirge's Kickin' Chimaerok Chops!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.6,"y":28.1,"n":"Dirge Quikcleave","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"906":{"id":906,"t":"Betrayal from Within","lv":25,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Lok's Skull to Thork at the Crossroads in the Barrens.\nLok's Skull Lok Orcbane\nProvided: Lok's Skull","desc":"Take Lok's head to Thork in the Crossroads, ‹race›. <snort> He should know what has happened to my tribe without any words--ha, not that he would believe Mangletooth helped in <snort> such things. But I am sure he'll reward you for carrying out such a great deed. <snort>\nI will continue to bless you with Agamaggan's power for as long as I remain in this cage, ‹race›. Until then, farewell.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBarkshell Tunic Dry Moss Tunic\nExperience: 3,050\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Yes, what is it?","done":"You found the Razormane leader and killed him yourself, ‹name›? Amazing.\nI am without words, but that does not mean I am without thanks. The people of the Crossroads would do well to respect your strength.\nI must admit, I thought the leader of these raids on our supply lines was another quilboar. Thank you again, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.5,"y":59.3,"n":"Mangletooth","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.5,"y":30.9,"n":"Thork","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1066":{"id":1066,"t":"Blood of Innocents","lv":23,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Vials of Innocent Blood to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\n5 Vial of Innocent Blood Syndicate Shadow Mage 80 %","desc":"I will create a toxin to bleed the violence from the Venture Company, rendering them weak and docile. That should fix the Horde's problem in Stonetalon, yes?\nBut to create the toxin, I will need the blood of innocents, a difficult ingredient to obtain.\nFortunately the Syndicate, a group of human brigands in this area, employ shadow mages... and those mages collect innocent blood for their own, unsavory purposes.\nYou can find the Syndicate shadow mages in Durnholde Keep to the southeast.","rew":"Experience: 1,850\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Did you find the Syndicate Shadow Mages, and collect from them the blood?","done":"Very good! I trust the Syndicate gave you little trouble?\nAs I mentioned, the blood of innocents is not an easy thing to obtain. We are lucky the Syndicate shadow mages did the difficult work for us.\nNow hold a moment while I create my concoction...","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"3786":{"id":3786,"t":"Morrowgrain Research","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use an Evergreen Pouch with a Packet of Tharlendis Seeds and two Un'Goro Soil samples to try and cultivate samples of Morrowgrain.\nBring 10 Morrowgrain to Bashana Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.\n10 Morrowgrain\nProvided: Evergreen Pouch","desc":"Here's your Evergreen Pouch that you'll need to use the Tharlendis seeds with. You also need to have Un'Goro soil samples on hand to use as fertilizer for the seeds. Just use the pouch when you have everything; the pouch will take care of the rest.\nWhen you have enough morrowgrain, bring them to me here on Elder Rise. Please don't bother the Arch Druid; he'll be very busy with the research, as well as the multitude of concerns he has!","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Circle Cache\nExperience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Yes ‹name›, have you grown some morrowgrain for the Arch Druid's important research? The mysterious properties of Un'Goro Crater become clearer with each passing day, thanks to the help you are giving us.","done":"Well done ‹name›, I will be sure to give these to the Arch Druid himself when he has need of them. Meanwhile, please accept this as a token of the Cenarion Circle's appreciation.\nOur need for morrowgrain, for now, is constant; if you wish to continue aiding us, then please return when you have cultivated more of it.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":34.2,"n":"Bashana Runetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"426":{"id":426,"t":"The Mills Overrun","lv":8,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 5 Notched Ribs and 3 Blackened Skulls, then return to Deathguard Dillinger in Brill.\n5 Notched Rib Cracked Skull Soldier 40 % , Rattlecage Soldier 40 %\n3 Blackened Skull Darkeye Bonecaster 40 %","desc":"The Scourge are trying to form a base at the Agamand Mills. If they do, then they can stage further attacks within Tirisfal.\nThe orders have been given. The Scourge in the Mills must be destroyed.\nGo to the Mills. Collect Notched Ribs from Rattlecage and Cracked Skull Soldiers, and Blackened Skulls from Darkeye Bonecasters.\nTo get to the Mills, follow the road west. After crossing the bridge, take the next fork north then keep going north. When you see windmills, the battle will begin.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCryptwalker Boots Sturdy Cloth Trousers\nMoney: 4 50 0 gold, 4 silver, 50 copper Experience: 875\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Our battles with the Scourge wage on, ‹name›. Do your part and throw those cursed, mindless undead back into the Plaguelands!","done":"Your efforts in the war are felt among us, ‹name›. I will not thank you for doing what is necessary, but the Deathguards of Tirisfal will remember your name.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":58.2,"y":51.4,"n":"Deathguard Dillinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"7626":{"id":7626,"t":"Bell of Dethmoora","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Elixirs of Shadow Power to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.\n10 Elixir of Shadow Power","desc":"A Bell of Dethmoora, named after the late warlock Dethmoora Darkeyes, is one of the three tools needed to create a Circle of Greater Summoning. When properly atuned with the Wheel and the Candle, these items conduct vast stores of arcane power.\nMy servant Gorzeeki can construct such a bell, but to do so he will need a large supply of elixirs of shadow power. Procure the elixirs from an alchemist and bring them to Gorzeeki.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"You have those elixirs, ‹name›? Mor'zul told me you need a Bell of Dethmoora, and making one of those takes a lot of shadow power!","done":"Very good! I hope these elixirs weren't too hard to get. Sometimes alchemists can be so miserly with their creations...\nI'll make the bell and keep it until you're ready for your ritual.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.7,"y":31.6,"n":"Mor'zul Bloodbringer","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Gorzeeki Wildeyes","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1706":{"id":1706,"t":"Grimand's Armor","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nFire Hardened Coif\nExperience: 3,050","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":59.7,"y":33.8,"n":"Grimand Elmore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8426":{"id":8426,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"8266":{"id":8266,"t":"Ribbons of Sacrifice","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 39. Gives 650 experience instead of 9,500, 0.07 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Ribbons of Sacrifice to Captain Shatterskull so that the Outriders may reward you for acting on our behalf.\nWarsong Gulch Ribbon of Sacrifice","desc":"I understand that it can be difficult at times to come out on top in Warsong Gulch. Still, your effort on our behalf - even when victory is not achieved - is important.\nShould you complete one of the trials inside Warsong Gulch and not achieve victory, you will still receive a Ribbons of Sacrifice. Bring it to me so that the Outriders may reward you for acting on our behalf... even if you weren't able to win this time.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","done":"Well, you did not flee in the face of defeat. You stood your ground, ‹name›, and when it comes right down to it, that is what makes for a true hero. No doubt you will win next time... but nonetheless we thank you for your effort.\nLevel 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Horde Shareable No Quest ID 8266","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"4986":{"id":4986,"t":"Glyphed Oaken Branch","lv":56,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Based on the magic enchanted within the Glyphed Oaken Branch, its delivery to the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus is the next step the tauren druid sought. Seek one of the druids there for assistance.\nGlyphed Oaken Branch\nProvided: Glyphed Oaken Branch","desc":"The lifeless hand of the tauren druid clutches a surprisingly healthy looking oaken branch. Examining the branch reveals glyphs of a druidic nature carved into the bark.\nAs you grasp the branch, you notice it is warm to the touch, more than it should be. The image of the Teldrassil tree enters your mind - Darnassus specifically - and the words \"Cenarion Circle\" are on the tip of your tongue. It would appear that the suggestion of where to take the branch has been placed within it.","rew":"You will receive:\nCerise Drape\nExperience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"On behalf of the Cenarion Circle, I bid you welcome to this enclave, ‹class›. What business do you have with us?","done":"This... this is quite strange. This druid - this tauren druid no less - entrusted you with a great deal of valuable information on the extent of the Scourge's plague. I am surprised a tauren would give a ‹race› such information, and freely at that if what you say is true. We will make good use of this, I promise you. Perhaps the tauren have not fallen as far from Cenarius as Fandral would believe...\nErm, anyway, please - accept this as a token of thanks from the Cenarion Circle.\nWestern Plaguelands Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":53.7,"y":64.7,"n":"Mulgris Deepriver","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5226":{"id":5226,"t":"Return to Chillwind Point","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Return to Chillwind Point.","obj":"Bring the Filled Gahrron's Withering Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\nFilled Gahrron's Withering Bottle\nProvided: Filled Gahrron's Withering Bottle","desc":"You carefully close the spigot in the control panel, watching the cauldron's putrid ichors drip into the empty bottle.\nWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp to complete the mission.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,100\n+50 reputation with Stormwind\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Gahrron's Withering houses the last cauldron here in the west that we need access to. Once we have a sample of the plague it spews forth, we will be able to introduce our reagents into the environment through four separate vessels! The Scourge will be hard pressed to keep us out of all four, even with the power of Kel'Thuzad behind them.","done":"Congratulations ‹name›, you've unlocked the last cauldron for us! Alchemist Arbington will soon know what this cauldron requires as far as reagents needed for the mix.\nAs for you, I am sure that Commander Valorfist will want to thank you personally for the assistance you've given us. Without you, our struggle against the Scourge would have been nearly insurmountable. Thank you, hero!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":62.5,"y":58.5,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":84.5,"n":"High Priestess MacDonnell","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"8186":{"id":8186,"t":"Death's Embrace","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring me thise things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!\nPrimal Hakkari Idol\nPunctured Voodoo Doll\nPrimal Hakkari Idol Jin'do the Hexxer in Zul'Gurub , Bloodlord Mandokir in Zul'Gurub\nPunctured Voodoo Doll Gurubashi Headhunter 0.1 % in Zul'Gurub , Zulian Cub 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Witch Doctor 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Voodoo Slave 0 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"Zanza can create the ancient troll enchantments with the right components. The first is a primal Hakkari idol that must be taken from the most powerful of the Hakkari lieutenants: Jin'do and the Bloodlord.\nThe second is a punctured voodoo doll. These can be found in the piles of refuse that litter this foul place. Look inside the jinxed hoodoo.\nBring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nDeath's Embrace\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Bring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","done":"Use it well, ‹class›. Show the Hakkari no mercy!\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8186","cats":["zulgurub"]},"8106":{"id":8106,"t":"Kezan's Taint","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","rew":"You will receive:\nKezan's Taint\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","done":"Accept this talisman, ‹class›. Accept it and use its power to strike down our mutual enemies.\nKnow that around your neck you carry a piece of history. Kezan was once a grand territory of the Zandalar Empire. Alas, the taint of goblin trade princes would force out my proud brothers and sisters.\nKezan is now home to the goblin capital of the Undermine; but know that before the taint, it held greatness. Still to this day Kezan is considered sacred land to my people.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});